-- Generated by scripts/dump-defs.ts from the TypeScript definitions.
-- Do not edit: run `npm run defs` instead.
--
-- Said twice, on purpose. `npm run defs` stamped the same statement
-- `20260916153607_defs.sql`, and the hand-written migration beside it was
-- stamped `20260916160000` — so the generated one sorted *before* a migration
-- the project had already run, and the ordering guard in `island.yml` refused
-- the commit. Renaming it would have meant rewriting a commit already on the
-- branch, so it stands where it is and this carries the same line at a stamp
-- that sorts after everything on the project.
--
-- Costs nothing: `create or replace function` is idempotent, this one has no
-- dependencies, and both copies sort before the migration that reads it.
create or replace function coax_step() returns double precision language sql immutable as $fn$ select 0.03::double precision $fn$;
